{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",

    /* Was `"moduleResolution": "node"` (node10). TypeScript 6 deprecates that
       with an error and 7 removes it, so this is the migration rather than an
       `ignoreDeprecations` line that only buys the 6.x window. `bundler` is
       the honest description of how this workspace actually resolves: nothing
       here is emitted by tsc — the apps run under tsx, the web app is built by
       Vite — so module specifiers are resolved by a bundler or a loader, never
       by node's own algorithm against tsc output.

       `allowImportingTsExtensions` follows from that. Under `bundler`, a
       dependency that ships raw TypeScript (`jmap-rfc-types`) resolves to its
       `.ts` sources, whose own imports carry the extension; node10 resolution
       never reached them. It is safe only because every config here sets
       `noEmit` — tsc refuses the option otherwise — and it permits nothing at
       runtime that tsx and Vite did not already accept. */
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,

    /* Each of the three below was measured against the whole workspace before
       being turned on, and each reported ZERO errors — they cost nothing today
       and are here to keep it that way.

       `isolatedModules` is the load-bearing one. Nothing here is compiled by
       tsc; the apps run under tsx and the web app is built by Vite, and BOTH
       transpile one file at a time with esbuild, which never sees the rest of
       the program. That is precisely the model isolatedModules describes, so
       without it tsc was type-checking under assumptions the actual runtime
       does not make. apps/web already set it; the workspace did not.

       `noImplicitOverride` and `noFallthroughCasesInSwitch` are ordinary
       correctness checks. apps/web had the second one, the packages did not —
       the same one-config-knows, the-other-does-not split. */
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "types": ["node"],
    "noEmit": true,

    /* Every construct here must be removable by deleting characters — no
       enums, no namespaces, no parameter properties.

       NOT because the current runtime cannot handle those. `tsx` (esbuild)
       TRANSFORMS as well as erases, so it happily emits the constructor
       assignments a parameter property implies; the 45 this repo had all
       worked. What cannot handle them is a PURE eraser, and Node's own type
       stripping is one — checked rather than assumed:

           class C { constructor(private readonly x: number) {} }
           node --experimental-strip-types  ->  SyntaxError
           tsx                              ->  runs

       So this option is what makes `node src/index.ts` a possible runtime for
       this workspace instead of `tsx src/index.ts`. It does not take that step
       — the apps still run under tsx — it removes the reason they had to.

       Turning it on meant rewriting those 45 parameter properties into
       explicit fields, done mechanically through the TypeScript AST so that
       defaults, optional markers and `super()` ordering survived. */
    "erasableSyntaxOnly": true,
    "paths": {
      "@openmig/managed": ["./packages/managed/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/managed/*": ["./packages/managed/src/*"],
      "@openmig/shared": ["./packages/shared/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/shared/*": ["./packages/shared/src/*"],
      "@openmig/ledger": ["./packages/ledger/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/ledger/*": ["./packages/ledger/src/*"],
      "@openmig/core": ["./packages/core/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/core/*": ["./packages/core/src/*"],
      "@openmig/orchestration": ["./packages/orchestration/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/orchestration/*": ["./packages/orchestration/src/*"],
      "@openmig/scheduler/in-process": ["./packages/scheduler/src/scheduler.ts"],
      "@openmig/connectors": ["./packages/connectors/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/connectors/*": ["./packages/connectors/src/*"],
      "@openmig/engines": ["./packages/engines/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/engines/*": ["./packages/engines/src/*"],
      "@openmig/scheduler": ["./packages/scheduler/src/index.ts"],
      "@openmig/scheduler/*": ["./packages/scheduler/src/*"],
      "@openmig/testing": ["./packages/testing/src/testcontainers-setup.ts"],
      "@openmig/testing/*": ["./packages/testing/src/*"]
    }
  }
}
